; Production streaming-target proof memory map.
;
; The active compiler has no generated-image or rollback staging region. The
; two released 4 KiB ranges remain named only so the proof profile can account
; for the recovered Z80 address space explicitly.

MMCORE     EQU $0000

; The debug compiler is a host-only instrumented image and has its own symbol
; map. Its trace instructions may extend beyond the historical 16 KiB size.
MMCORLIM   EQU $6000

; These addresses are one hosted deployment policy, not properties of the
; compiler code. CompilerCoreBase may be relocated independently; a deployment
; must choose non-overlapping code, workspace, source, target and stack ranges.
; Keep the mutable compiler workspace well above the current hosted image so a
; feature cannot silently turn a small size increase into state corruption.
MMWORK     EQU $6000
MMWRKLIM   EQU $7000
MMSOURCE   EQU $7000
MMSRCLIM   EQU $7800
; The native source provider reuses the old resident-source window as two
; bounded host buffers. Token scratch admits the longest raw string token;
; the following chunk window is refilled without retaining the complete unit.
MMTOKEN    EQU MMSOURCE
MMTOKEND   EQU MMSOURCE+$0500
SRCCHUNK   EQU MMTOKEND
MMCHKEND   EQU MMSRCLIM

MMRGEN     EQU MMSRCLIM
MMRGNEND   EQU MMSRCLIM

; These proof-only fixtures are not one simultaneously loaded source window.
; Each compile still observes SourceLimit-SourceBase; this retained corpus only
; lets one proof exercise several independent projects without self-modifying.
MMCORP     EQU $7800
MMCORPEN   EQU $7B00

; The proof driver follows the selected proof runtime in this reservation.
; Neither range is part of the compiler's deployment ABI.
MMRUN      EQU MMCORPEN
MMRUNEND   EQU $8900

MMEXEC     EQU $8900
MMEXEND    EQU $9900

MMDATA     EQU MMEXEC+$0100
MMDATEND   EQU MMDATA+$0400
MMBSS      EQU MMDATEND
MMBSSEND   EQU MMBSS+$0400
MMREGEND   EQU MMBSSEND
MMREGCAP   EQU MMREGEND-MMDATA
RORDCAP    EQU $0400

MMSERV     EQU $9900
MMSRVEND   EQU $A000

; Proof-state and spare describe the high proof adapter/log policy. The actual
; driver follows RuntimeCodeEnd because the saved logs occupy this range.
MMPROOF    EQU $A000
MMPREND    EQU $A800
MMSPARE    EQU $A800
MMRBACK    EQU $B000
MMRBKEND   EQU $C000
MMSPEND    EQU $F000

MMSTKBOT   EQU $F000
STACKTOP   EQU $FF00

MMHIGH     EQU $FF00
; Highest address is a native word; host output reports its exclusive end +1.
MMLAST     EQU $FFFF
